cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AnCiR, please cite this record. The companion handbook is a
  separate work with its own DOI (10.5281/zenodo.21727169); if you are citing
  the handbook rather than the software, cite that instead. See the references
  section below.
title: "AnCiR: Analysis of Chronobiological Rhythms"
abstract: >-
  AnCiR is a graphical, no-coding tool for the analysis of chronobiological
  rhythms and other time-series data. It provides periodicity detection
  (Sokolove-Bushell chi-squared, Enright, Lomb-Scargle, FFT), cosinor and
  harmonic-cosinor fitting, non-parametric circadian rhythm analysis
  (IS, IV, RA, M10, L5), circular statistics, continuous wavelet transforms,
  smoothing, and inferential statistics with multiple-comparison correction
  and surrogate or permutation nulls.

  This repository also holds the source of A Handbook of Chronobiological Data
  Analysis, an interactive companion text with worked examples and animations
  that explains the methods and shows how to carry them out in AnCiR. The
  handbook is archived as a separate Zenodo record (10.5281/zenodo.21727169)
  so that it can be cited at its own version, and is published at
  https://ancir.pages.dev/handbook.html.
